1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,800
What's up everybody, welcome back to the channel. Today we are building a full castle in survival, no creative mode.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
And um, I gave myself one rule. I only get three in-game days to finish it.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,800
If the sun comes up on day four and the castle isn't done, I tear the whole thing down.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,800
So uh, no pressure at all. Let's get into it.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,800
Okay so day one. First thing I need is stone, and a lot of it. Like, a ridiculous amount of stone.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,800
I worked it out before recording. The castle plan needs about two thousand blocks of cobblestone.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,800
That is around thirty one stacks, which is uh, way more than I have ever mined in one go.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,800
So I am heading down to this ravine I found yesterday because it has a ton of exposed stone on the walls.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,800
Quick tip here, if you are mining a lot of stone, put Efficiency on your pickaxe before anything else.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,800
It sounds obvious but it cuts the mining time almost in half, and on a three day timer that matters a lot.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,800
I don't have Efficiency yet, so um, I am doing this the slow way. Pray for me.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,800
Okay this is going pretty well actually. I have about eight stacks already and it is still only morning.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,800
Wait. Wait wait wait. Do you hear that? That hissing?

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,800
No. No no no. Get away from me. Get away!

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,800
It blew up the whole wall. I lost, I lost like four stacks of cobblestone. They went into the lava.

16
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,800
That creeper just cost me an hour of mining. I am not even, I am not even mad. I am just impressed.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,800
Okay, lesson learned. Always light up the area you are mining in, even during the day, because ravines stay dark.

18
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,800
Let's place some torches and um, try this again.

19
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,800
Alright, it's the end of day one. Final count is twenty two stacks of cobblestone, which is behind schedule.

20
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,800
So tomorrow I need to mine faster and build at the same time. That's the plan.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,800
Day two. I am up early and I am starting with the foundation, because a castle is only as good as its base.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,800
The footprint is forty one by forty one blocks. I like odd numbers because then there is a true middle block for the gate.

23
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,800
I am marking the corners first with wool so I can see the shape from far away.

24
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:39,800
Then I fill in the outline with stone bricks. I crafted the bricks from the cobblestone using a stonecutter.

25
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,800
Another tip, the stonecutter is way cheaper than crafting stairs and walls on a table. One block in, one block out.

26
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,800
With a crafting table you lose blocks on every stair recipe, so uh, use the stonecutter. Trust me.

27
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:03,800
Okay the outline is done. Now the walls. I am going nine blocks high with a little lip at the top for the battlements.

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:10,800
This part is honestly kind of relaxing. You just place block after block and put on some music.

29
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,800
I am mixing in some cobblestone and mossy stone so the wall doesn't look flat. Texture is everything in a build.

30
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,800
See how it breaks up the wall? From far away it looks old, like it has been standing for a hundred years.

31
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,800
Okay, the four corner towers. These are going to be round, which is um, harder than it sounds in a block game.

32
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,800
I am using a circle generator website for the shape. It is eleven blocks wide.

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,800
Placing round towers by hand is the the slowest part of this whole build. Every layer has to match.

34
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,800
And I just realized I built the first tower one block off. The whole thing is crooked.

35
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:59,800
Yeah. Yeah, it's crooked. I have to take down six layers. This is fine. This is totally fine.

36
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,800
Okay, fixed. It's straight now. I am going to pretend that never happened.

37
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,800
It's the end of day two and the walls are up, three towers are up, and I'm almost out of stone again.

38
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:19,800
And I still haven't started the keep, the big building in the middle. So uh, day three is going to be tight.

39
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,800
Day three. Final day. If this isn't done by sunrise tomorrow, it all comes down.

40
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,800
Plan for today: finish the last tower, build the keep, and make the gate. That's a lot.

41
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:40,800
Last tower goes up quick because I finally know what I'm doing. Practice really does make perfect.

42
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,800
Now the keep. I am making it two stories with a big hall on the ground floor and a bedroom on top.

43
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,800
For the roof I am using dark oak stairs. Dark oak with stone is my favorite combo in the whole game.

44
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,800
The contrast just looks so good. Dark wood, grey stone, a little bit of moss. Chef's kiss.

45
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:08,800
Okay it is noon on day three and the keep has walls and a roof. Now the inside.

46
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:15,800
I am going simple inside. Long tables, banners on the walls, and um, a big fireplace at the end.

47
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:23,800
For the fireplace I use campfires under a chimney of stone bricks. The smoke goes straight up through it. Looks amazing.

48
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,800
Okay, gate time. This is the part I have been most excited about.

49
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:36,800
The gate is a working drawbridge made with sticky pistons. Redstone is not my strong point, so uh, wish me luck.

50
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:43,800
The idea is you press one button and the bridge pulls back and a wall of blocks closes the entrance.

51
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,800
Let's test it. Button, and.

52
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,800
Nothing. Absolutely nothing happened.

53
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,800
Okay I found it. I had one repeater facing the wrong way. One repeater.

54
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,800
Let's try again. Button, and. Yes! Yes! It works! Look at that!

55
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:08,800
That is the best thing I have ever built with redstone. I am so proud of this little bridge.

56
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,800
Okay the sun is starting to go down on day three. I have maybe five minutes of daylight left.

57
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:22,800
Last things. Torches on the walls so mobs don't spawn inside, and the banners on the towers.

58
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:29,800
It's getting dark. I am placing the last banner. And, done. Done! The castle is done!

59
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:35,800
With about thirty seconds of daylight to spare. That was way too close.

60
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:42,800
Okay let's do the tour. We start at the drawbridge, which still works, I checked it like ten times.

61
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:50,800
Through the gate you have the courtyard. I added a small farm and a well in here so you could actually live in it.

62
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:57,800
The four towers each have a ladder to the top. From up here you can see the whole valley.

63
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:04,800
And then the keep. Great hall with the fireplace, and up the stairs, the bedroom with a view of the gate.

64
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:11,800
Let's go up on the wall at night. This is my favorite view. All the torches on the walls glowing.

65
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,800
Honestly I didn't think I could do this in three days. On day one when the creeper hit, I was ready to quit.

66
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:26,800
So final numbers. About two thousand three hundred blocks placed, one creeper disaster, and one crooked tower.

67
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:32,800
And one drawbridge that works on the second try, which for me is a record.

68
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:39,800
If you want the build plans, I put the measurements for the towers and the keep in the description.

69
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,800
Let me know in the comments what I should build next with a time limit. Maybe a city? A ship?

70
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,800
If you liked this, you know, hit subscribe. It really helps the channel.

71
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Thanks for watching, and I'll see you in the next one. Peace.

